NNAAMMEE
       lsirq - utility to display kernel interrupt information

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       llssiirrqq [options]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       Display kernel interrupt counter information.

       The default output is subject to change. So whenever possible, you
       should avoid using default outputs in your scripts. Always explicitly
       define expected columns by using ----oouuttppuutt.

OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       --nn, ----nnoohheeaaddiinnggss
           Don’t print headings.

       --oo, ----oouuttppuutt _l_i_s_t
           Specify which output columns to print. Use ----hheellpp to get a list of
           all supported columns. The default list of columns may be extended
           if list is specified in the format _+_l_i_s_t.

       --ss, ----ssoorrtt _c_o_l_u_m_n
           Specify sort criteria by column name. See ----hheellpp output to get
           column names.

       --JJ, ----jjssoonn
           Use JSON output format.

       --PP, ----ppaaiirrss
           Produce output in the form of key="value" pairs. All potentially
           unsafe characters are hex-escaped (\x<code>).

       --SS, ----ssooffttiirrqq
           Show softirqs information.

       --hh, ----hheellpp
           Display help text and exit.

       --VV, ----vveerrssiioonn
           Print version and exit.

